INSERT INTO houses (id, street, house_type, neighborhood_id, realtor_id, rooms, bedrooms, house_square, price, is_rent_house, description)
VALUES
    (31,'Kattenburgerhof', 'APARTMENT', 1, 1, 4, 3, 103, 750, true,
     E'Looking for a well-laid-out maisonette apartment with 3 bedrooms, a sunny southeast-facing balcony, and an elevator?\n'
     'This modern 4-room apartment offers the perfect combination of comfort, space, and an ideal location—it has everything you''re looking for!\n\n'
     'The maisonette boasts a living area of approximately 103 sqm (NEN-2580) and is situated on the third and fourth floors of a well-maintained complex. With a spacious balcony offering delightful views, it’s the perfect spot to relax. Additionally, there’s a private storage space on the ground floor.\n\n'
     'Located in a car-free, quiet, and open area, but just minutes away from the vibrant city center with its lovely shops, boutiques, restaurants, and cafés, this property provides the best of both worlds: tranquility and lively surroundings.'),
    (32,'Kantershof', 'APARTMENT', 1, 2, 4, 3, 92, 475, true,
     E'Located in the lively Amsterdam-Zuidoost in the popular Kantershof neighborhood, this recently completely renovated family home awaits you. Kantershof was created in the 1970s as part of the renewal of Amsterdam-Zuidoost. The neighborhood is known for its characteristic courtyard structure and green, child-friendly living environment. What once started as a progressive concept for quiet living in the middle of the city, has grown into a warm neighborhood with a strong sense of community.\n\n'
     'This home is immediately habitable and offers comfortable living with plenty of opportunities for expansion. You can enjoy the deep backyard, a quiet living environment and the convenience of perpetual leasehold in a neighborhood that exudes both history and coziness.\n\n'
     'With a generous living area of approximately 92 m², this house offers an oasis of peace and style. Upon entering, you are welcomed in a bright living room with a view of the backyard of no less than 46 m², situated on the northeast. The living room connects seamlessly to the kitchen, which is equipped with all basic appliances. The ground floor also has a separate toilet and handy storage cupboards.\n\n'
     'On the first floor there are three cosy bedrooms and a modern bathroom that is fully equipped for your comfort. The spacious layout and practical landing make this an ideal living space for families or couples. The house also offers possibilities for expansion so that you can increase the living space as desired.'),
    (33,'Leusdenhof', 'APARTMENT', 1, 3, 2, 1, 96, 570, true,
     E'Unique opportunity! Affordable living in a green and peaceful area of Amsterdam. This conveniently located 2-room apartment on the first floor is wonderfully spacious and features a large balcony with a view of a lush, green environment. There''s plenty of potential to style and arrange the home according to your own ideas. Feeling inspired yet? Then this apartment is perfect for you. Around the property, there is ample parking, and you’ll always have your own designated parking spot!\n\n'
     'We take you through:\n• Living pleasure: 61.8 m2\n• Available right away!\n• Furniture is negotiable\n• Quiet location in green surroundings\n• Bright living room with open kitchen (1980)\n• Sanitary facilities including a bath (1980)\n• Opportunity for own layout and styling\n• Spacious bedroom\n• Large, partly covered balcony with open views\n• Ample parking space\n• Let''s show you around!'),
    (34,'Vancouverstraat', 'APARTMENT', 1, 4, 3, 2, 59, 500, true,
     E'Charming groud floor property on Vancouverstraat – ready for your personal touch!\n\n'
     'Welcome to this partially renovated home in the popular Vancouverstraat area of Amsterdam! Offering ample space, comfort, and a clever layout, this property also features a spacious outdoor area. Finish the remaining details to your liking and create your dream home. Interested? Schedule a viewing today and discover all the possibilities!\n\n'
     'Ground Floor\nThe entrance leads to a bright, open living room with a kitchen. The modern kitchen is fully equipped with a dishwasher, fridge with freezer compartment, induction hob, and built-in extractor fan – a perfect blend of style and functionality.\n\n'
     'From the living room, you access a separate toilet with a small sink, a practical storage room housing the central heating system, the utility panel, and connections for the washing machine. At the rear of the property, there are two bedrooms, each with its own private bathroom.\n\n'
     'The bathrooms are fully finished and include a toilet, washbasin, towel radiator, mechanical ventilation, shower, and mirror. A practical and private setup!'),
    (35,'Arent Janszoon Ernststraat', 'APARTMENT', 1, 5, 4, 3, 80, 450, true,
    E'Well-designed and spacious 4-room apartment (approx. 80 m²) with sunny balcony and storage room!\n\n'
     'This lovely apartment, located on the second floor, offers a beautiful view over a park and has an excellent location near the Zuidas and the Groot Gelderlandplein. With a surface area of ??approx. 80 m², a practical layout, a sunny balcony facing south and a storage room on the ground floor, this is an ideal home for those who want to live comfortably and centrally.'
     'Layout:\nVia the communal entrance you reach the hall of this well-designed apartment. The bright living room with access to the sunny balcony (south) forms the heart of the home. Adjacent is a spacious bedroom. At the front are two additional bedrooms and a functional kitchen, equipped with a 4-burner gas hob, fridge-freezer and oven.\n\n'
     'The bathroom is efficiently designed with a sink, walk-in shower and connections for a washing machine and dryer. Furthermore, the home has a separate toilet and a handy storage room with the boiler for hot water. On the ground floor there is an extra storage room of approx. 5 m².'),
    (36,'Tollensstraat', 'APARTMENT', 1, 6, 2, 1, 43, 400, true,
    E'Turn-key apartment of approximately 43 m² with 1 bedroom, balcony, and perpetual ground lease paid off!\nThis cleverly designed apartment was renovated in 2020 and features an open kitchen with built-in appliances, a luxurious bathroom, a bedroom at the rear (with the option for a second bedroom), a sunny balcony, a separate toilet, and a spacious attic storage room. Come and see it quickly, because this is a home you don''t want to miss!\n\n'
     'Location and Accessibility:\nThe location is very central, in the sought-after Oud-West district, right on the edge of the city center. Within walking distance, you''ll find the popular Vondelpark, shopping streets such as Kinkerstraat, Jan Pieter Heijestraat, and Overtoom, as well as various bakeries, supermarkets, and the Ten Kate Market. This location offers the best of both worlds – the vibrant atmosphere of the city center and the unique charm of Oud-West.'
     'Nearby hotspots include Café Lennep, Pizza Project, and Barrica Food Bar. Additionally, "De Hallen" with its food halls, restaurants, cinema, and various shops is just around the corner. This location guarantees a wide variety of shops, cafés, and restaurants. The neighborhood also offers numerous amenities such as schools, childcare facilities, and cultural venues. Thanks to its central location in Amsterdam, nearly everything is reachable within 10 minutes by bike. Public transport and car accessibility are excellent as well, with various bus and tram lines within walking distance and quick access to the A-10 ring road.'),
    (37,'Voordek', 'APARTMENT', 1, 7, 4, 3, 87, 400, true,
    E'Unique living in peaceful Amsterdam Noord: a move-in-ready home in a perfect location!\n\n'
     'Located in a family-friendly and desirable neighborhood in Amsterdam Noord, this beautiful 5-room apartment on the first floor boasts a fresh and modern look thanks to recent updates and a well-thought-out layout. Additionally, the ground lease has been fully paid off, making this home even more attractive.\n\n'
     'Upon entering the spacious hallway, you immediately notice how well the apartment has been maintained. The hallway provides access to the bright living room, three comfortable bedrooms, the neatly tiled bathroom, separate toilet, and the cozy kitchen. The kitchen is well-maintained and equipped with modern appliances, including an induction hob, oven, dishwasher, and fridge with freezer compartment. The apartment features a stylish laminate floor, and all interior doors were renewed in 2024. Moreover, the entire interior has been freshly painted, making it ready for immediate move-in.\n\n'
     'The bathroom stands out with its floor-to-ceiling tiling and is equipped with a shower, modern sink cabinet, and washing machine connection. It offers everything you need for comfort and relaxation.'),
    (38,'Nicolaas Witsenkade', 'APARTMENT', 1, 8, 3, 2, 71, 770, true,
    E'Beautifully renovated 3-room apartment with a living area of approx. 71 m² (gross 105 m2!) and a view of the water, located in a prime location between the Pijp and the Weteringschans.\n\n'
     'Very well-maintained communal entrance on the ground floor. Neat and spacious staircase to the second floor.\n'
     'Private staircase to the third floor. Beautiful front door with beautiful fittings, hall, access to the living room. Luxurious well-equipped open kitchen (including Quooker, Siemens combi oven, induction). Spacious living room with herringbone floor, air conditioning and strikingly beautiful ridge height with beam details. Phenomenal view over the water and the bridge to the Van Woustraat. Separate toilet in the hall, space for washing/drying, bathroom and two bedrooms. The bathroom has a spacious walk-in shower and washbasin with furniture. The two well-sized bedrooms both have space for wardrobes or a nice sitting area. The master bedroom has a large window, overlooking the quiet courtyards.\n\n'
     'The whole is luxuriously and tastefully renovated. In the details you can see the choice for high-quality materials. Quality is paramount here and you feel that right away!'),
    (39,'Nicolaas Witsenkade', 'APARTMENT', 1, 9, 2, 1, 46, 540, true,
    E'Beautifully renovated 2-room apartment with a living area of approx. 46 m² and a view of the quiet courtyards, located in a prime location between the Pijp and the Weteringschans.\n\n'
     'Very well-maintained communal entrance on the ground floor. The apartment is located on the first floor. Beautiful front door with beautiful fittings, hall, access to the living room. Luxurious well-equipped open kitchen (including Quooker, Siemens combi oven, induction). Spacious living room with herringbone floor and high ceiling. Separate toilet in the hall. Large bedroom with enough space for wardrobes and a luxurious en-suite bathroom with walk-in shower and washbasin.\n\n'
     'The whole has been luxuriously and tastefully renovated. In the details you can see the choice for high-quality materials. Quality is paramount here and you can feel it immediately!'),
    (40,'Hectorstraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 10, 3, 2, 57, 550, true,
    E'This apartment, situated on the first floor and accessible via a well-maintained communal staircase, boasts a practical layout. Upon entering through the central hallway, you have access to all rooms. At the front of the apartment is the charming living room, featuring a characteristic fireplace and a convenient built-in closet. French doors open onto the first balcony, located at the front of the property. Adjacent to the living room is the first bedroom, also with French doors leading to the balcony. This room is stylishly separated by a steel sliding door.\n\n'
     'The kitchen, located at the rear of the apartment, is equipped with a 4-burner gas stove with extractor hood, an oven, a sink, a fridge-freezer combination, and ample storage space. From the kitchen, you have access to the second balcony, which offers enough space for a cozy seating area and/or a balcony bar. A practical storage closet is also located here. The second bedroom, accessible from the central hallway, also provides access to the second balcony via French doors. This well-proportioned bedroom features a spacious built-in wardrobe with extra storage space. The bathroom is centrally located and fitted with a shower, toilet, and washbasin unit.\n\n'
     'In short, this is a comfortable apartment with a well-thought-out layout, featuring two balconies that bring in plenty of natural light and create a spacious ambiance. An ideal home with numerous possibilities!'),
    (41,'Pieter Calandlaan', 'APARTMENT', 11, 11, 4, 3, 105, 450, true,
    E'On the 8th and top floor we can offer you this luxuriously finished corner apartment. The apartment is energy efficient, with an energy label A, has 3 bedrooms, a spacious terrace facing south, a Cinewall and a new herringbone floor. The three extra windows in the living room provide a lot of extra natural light in the house. The apartment is in a modern apartment complex with elevator and has a private storage room.\n\n'
     'The apartment is within walking distance of various shops (including supermarkets) on the Pieter Calandlaan and the Osdorpplein, excellent public transport connections with direct connection to the center of Amsterdam, the Sloterplas, theater de Meervaart and a variety of restaurants. By car, arterial roads (such as A10, A9, A4 and A5) are easily accessible.\n\n'
     'Special features:\n- 104.50m2 living space (Nen-2580);\n- Corner apartment;\n- Energy label A;\n- elevator;\n- leasehold bought off until 31-03-2055;\n- New and luxurious quality herringbone floor;\n- Active Owners Association, service costs €170,10,- p.m;\n- Apartment located on leasehold land (AB2000), canon has been bought off until 31 May 2055;\n- Possibility to rent parking space(s) in parking garage under complex;\n- Individual (bicycle) storage of approx. 3 m² in basement;\n- Spacious terrace of approx. 11 m² facing south;\n- Electric screens sun blinds in living room on south side.'),
     (42,'Groetstraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 12, 3, 2, 77, 425, true,
     E'Immediately habitable 3-room apartment with a storage room on the ground floor and a very spacious attic storage room in a green residential area.\n\n'
      'At the front a green courtyard with play area for the children.\nOn the ground floor a private bicycle shed.\n\n'
      'Layout of the house: entrance, hall, toilet, laundry room, kitchen with access to balcony at the front, neat bathroom with a luxurious finish, walk-in shower, double sink in furniture, beautiful mirror and towel radiator, two bedrooms at the rear, extended living room with dining area (this can easily be converted into a third bedroom)\nA large attic space in the roof.'),
      (43,'Czaar Peterstraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 13, 3, 2, 65, 450, true,
      E'This bright apartment is located in a prime location in the center of Amsterdam, on the trendy Czaar Peterstraat, right in the heart of the vibrant Eastern Docklands. The apartment was completely renovated in 2015, including foundation repairs, and converted into a spacious double upper house.\n\n'
       'Entrance through a shared door, stairs to the third floor. Entry on the third floor, through the private staircase, leading to the hallway on the fourth floor, from where all rooms are accessible.\n\n'
       'The spacious living room has windows at both the front and rear, allowing plenty of natural light. The living room also features an open kitchen equipped with a 5-burner gas stove, refrigerator, dishwasher, and a combination oven/microwave. Adjacent to the living room is the separate toilet and the first spacious bedroom.\n\n'
       'Through the hallway, you access the stairs to the fourth floor, which houses the second bedroom and bathroom. Both rooms are accessible via a landing. The bedroom is spacious enough for both a double bed and closet space. The bathroom is equipped with a vanity unit and a walk-in shower.'),
      (44,'Gulden Winckelplantsoen', 'APARTMENT', 10, 13, 3, 2, 60, 450, true,
      E'Characteristic and spacious 3-room apartment (60m2) with two balconies, two separate storage rooms and a beautiful view of a well-kept and wooded park directly at the Bos en Lommerplein.\n\n'
       'Ground floor:\nCommunal entrance to staircase and two storage rooms that belong to the house. One storage room is suitable as a bicycle cellar and the other as storage.\n\n'
       'Second floor:\nThrough the entrance you enter the hall that connects all rooms. At the front of the house is the spacious living room with the balcony facing west. Here you can sit in the sun until late in the evening in the summer. The side room is open and could also serve as a dining room or extra bedroom. From the living room you have a wide view over the Bos & Lommerplein. At the rear of the apartment are the two bedrooms and the kitchen. Through the kitchen and one of the bedrooms you have access to the second balcony. This is very spacious and recently renovated. The balcony is located on the east. Here you can enjoy your morning coffee in the sun. The bathroom has a sink, bath/shower and toilet.'),
      (45,'Eerste Atjehstraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 14, 3, 2, 57, 450, true,
      E'Well-maintained 3-room apartment on the first floor, with a practical layout and FREEHOLD.  The property has a sunny south-facing balcony which could possibly be increased in size, making it large enough for a dining table or a lounge sofa. The building was comprehensively renovated 20 years ago and split into 5 apartment rights; at which time all the windows were insulated. The property has energy label A. The Owners’ Association is active and has a multi-annual maintenance plan. All in all, a carefree 3-room apartment with a practical layout and a good standard of finish in a quiet street in the Indische Buurt area!'
       'Specifics\n- Year of construction: 1905\n- Living area: 57 m2( measurement report available)\n- The property is freehold\n- Split and thoroughly renovated in 2003\n- High ceilings (2.71m)\n- South-facing balcony\n- Double glazing in wooden frames at the front and PVC frames at the rear\n- New intercom system\n- Active Owners’ Association, 5 members\n- Energy label A\n- Quick delivery is possible\n- The owner previously let the apartment (non-resident occupancy clause)'),
      (46,'Van Bossestraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 15, 2, 1, 38, 350, true,
      E'What a lovely apartment! Situated on the first floor, this home offers a spacious bedroom, a bright living room with a cozy open kitchen, and a sunny west-facing balcony with unobstructed views. Owned land, so no ground lease, a well-managed and active HOA, and located in one of Amsterdam''s most charming neighborhoods. I warmly invite you to schedule a viewing.\n\n'
       'The Apartment:\nAs you enter on the first floor, you''ll immediately notice the abundance of natural light flooding the space. At the front of the apartment, you’ll find the bedroom, overlooking a quiet street with only local traffic. The bedroom is more than spacious enough to accommodate a double bed and a large wardrobe.\n\n'
       'The living area with its open kitchen is generously sized, neatly finished with plastered walls and an elegant laminate floor. The kitchen features a welcoming bar, ample storage and countertop space, and a range of appliances, including a new induction cooktop, extractor hood, fridge-freezer, dishwasher, and oven.\n\n'
       'The balcony offers unobstructed views, and its favorable west-facing position means you can enjoy the sun from afternoon until sunset.\n\nThe tidy bathroom is bright and fresh, equipped with a shower, toilet, and sink. Stylish shelves provide plenty of storage to keep things organized.'),
      (47,'Tommaso Albinonistraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 16, 3, 2, 121, 800, true,
      E'Welcome to Tommaso Albinonistraat 22 in Amsterdam.\nThis spacious, luxurious and bright apartment is located on the 2nd floor of the Eurocenter, which was completed in 2006, and has 2 spacious bedrooms, a spacious and bright living room, a bathroom, separate laundry room and a sunny balcony facing south. This apartment has a living area of no less than 121m2 and has an energy label A. Have we aroused your interest? Then contact us for a tour of this lovely apartment.\n\n'
       'Sellers speak:\nOur family has lived wonderfully in the Eurocenter for more than 10 years! However, it is now time for us to take the next step. We are sure that the next residents of this lovely apartment will also enjoy it here. Ideal access roads, just outside the ring road, but still close to the centre of Amsterdam. With tram 4 and RAI station around the corner, you are in the centre within 10 minutes. With Gelderlandplein a lovely shopping centre with the nicest shops. Although the street is busy, the neighborhood is surprisingly child-oriented with the Amstelpark and a nice primary school + daycare within 5 minutes walking distance.\n\n'
       'Layout:\nOn the ground floor of Eurocenter is the luxurious and spacious entrance with international appearance, where a caretaker is present every day (with the exception of the weekend). The entrance has a sitting area and a reading table for guests. The 2 elevators that provide access to the floors can be reached via the hall or the parking garage.'),
      (48,'Nassaukade', 'APARTMENT', 10, 17, 2, 1, 78, 600, true,
      E'Three-Room Apartment (78m²) with Balcony (6m²) on the First Floor and Storage Room (7m²) on the Fourth Floor. Private street entrance at the top of the portico. Beautiful original features. Elegant building from 1897, divided into apartments in 2004 and 2013. Professionally managed homeowners association (VvE). Leasehold prepaid until the end of 2054, with a favorable option to convert to perpetual leasehold. Unobstructed, spacious views at both the front and rear. Located at the edge of Oud-West and the city center (Jordaan), near Kinkerstraat and Elandsgracht.\n\n'
       'Behind the street entrance, there’s a vestibule and hallway. On the left side of the hall are the three rooms, while on the right are the toilet, bathroom, and a large closet with a washing machine connection. At the end of the hall is the kitchen. The rear-facing balcony is accessible from the kitchen and the adjacent room, offering summer sun from 12:30 PM to 8:00 PM. On the fourth floor, the apartment has its own private storage room, accessible via the right portico door and staircase.\n\n'
       'Nassaukade 320-1 is located on the border of Oud-West and the Jordaan, near Kinkerstraat and Elandsgracht. Cozy shops and supermarkets are just around the corner, along with an array of cosy and affordable restaurants, cafés, and hotspots (such as Waterkant and De Hallen). Both Westerpark and Vondelpark are nearby. Excellent public transport options include direct bus lines to Schiphol and Zandvoort, as well as convenient car access.\n\n'
       '* Spacious apartment of 78m²\n* Unobstructed, spacious views at the front and rear\n* West-southwest-facing balcony\n* Attic storage room\n* Leasehold prepaid until the end of 2054, favorable option to convert to perpetual leasehold\n* Professionally managed homeowners'' association (VvE)\n* Fantastic location on the border of Oud-West and Jordaan.'),
      (49,'Bethaniëndwarsstraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 18, 2, 1, 51, 800, true,
      E'Have you always dreamed of living in the heart of the capital? Then this is your chance.\nEntire building on a plot of land in full ownership.\n\n'
       'Within walking distance of everything important in the city.\n\nBusiness space:\nOn the ground floor you will find the business/storage space which is also suitable as a garage.\nThe entrance at the double door has a clear width of 2.30 meters, the rest of the facade is taken up by the entrance to the upper house\n\n'
       'House:\nFirst floor: bedroom and bathroom with bath, toilet and sink;\nSecond floor: living room with open kitchen, simple but practical, and access to roof terrace.\n\nSimple in finish but very practical in use and suitable for multiple layouts.\n\nImmediately available\nPart of a protected cityscape.'),
      (50,'Revaleiland', 'APARTMENT', 10, 19, 4, 3, 110, 775, true,
      E'Eco-friendly double ground floor apartment in Amsterdam Westelijke Houthavens\n\nWelcome to Revaleiland 33, a luxurious and sustainable home of 110 m², ideally located in the modern Westelijke Houthavens. This stylish double ground floor apartment offers a unique combination of comfort, tranquility and green living. With a terrace of 13 m² and access to a beautiful courtyard of 700 m², this is the perfect place for families or couples looking for a modern living environment.'
       'LAYOUT\nThe house is divided over two floors and has been cleverly laid out to make optimal use of the space. On the ground floor there is a spacious living room with a ceiling height of no less than 3.2 meters, which provides a feeling of light and space. The luxury kitchen is equipped with high-quality AEG appliances, a Quooker and stylish herringbone parquet floors with underfloor heating and cooling. Adjacent to the living room is a bright bedroom with an ensuite bathroom, equipped with a freestanding bath and a glass wall. From the dining area you have access to the 13 m² terrace, which directly borders the 700 m² communal courtyard.\n\n'
       'In the basement there are two spacious bedrooms, ideal as children''s, work or guest rooms. This floor has a second bathroom with a modern walk-in shower and a practical laundry room with extra storage space. Thanks to the clever layout, the house is not only functional, but also perfectly suited to a comfortable and luxurious lifestyle.\n\nThe house has exceptionally low energy costs and features with an EPC value of 0.14 (which is exceptionally environmentally friendly), 10 solar panels that contribute to its A++ energy label together with the district heating system which reflects the commitment to green living. The advanced Domotics system ensures easy and smart home management.\n\n'
       'The property also offers the possibility to buy the parking space for €60,000 euros in the underground garage and access to a bicycle shed. All of this is secured by a high-tech camera system and makes the total price for the house and parking space €835,000.'),
      (51,'Filips van Almondestraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 15, 3, 2, 55, 425, true,
      E'Atmospheric and charming 3-room apartment of 55 m² with a spacious balcony, situated in a prime location in De Baarsjes.\n\nThis modern and bright city apartment on the third floor combines style, comfort, and a smart layout. It features two well-sized bedrooms, a sunny living room with a bay window, a neat bathroom with a bathtub, a contemporary kitchen, a lovely balcony, and double glazing. All this ensures a delightful living experience.\n\n'
       'Location:\nThe property is located on Filips van Almondestraat, a quiet and cozy street between Witte de Withstraat and Admiralengracht, in the heart of vibrant Amsterdam West (De Baarsjes). Within walking distance, you''ll find Jan Evertsenstraat and Kinkerstraat, offering a wide range of cafés, restaurants, and shops, including Bar Baarsch, Radijs, Edel, Partisan, and Bar Spek. Supermarkets like Albert Heijn are also nearby. For relaxation, you can cycle to Vondelpark, Rembrandtpark, or Erasmuspark in just 10 minutes. Additionally, hotspots like De Hallen, the Ten Katemarkt, and the Jordaan are easily accessible.\n\n'
       'The accessibility is excellent: public transport to Central Station, Sloterdijk, and Lelylaan is well-organized, and by car, you can quickly reach the A10 ring road (exit S105). You can even moor a boat nearby on Admiralengracht.\n\n'
       'Layout:\nThrough the shared entrance, you reach the third floor. The apartment has a bright living room at the front with a charming bay window. The adjacent room, currently used as a dining room, is perfect as a second bedroom. The bathroom includes a bathtub, sink, and washing machine connection, and there is a separate toilet. The kitchen is modern and equipped with built-in appliances, including a fridge with freezer compartment, oven, gas stove, extractor hood, and dishwasher. From the kitchen, you access the balcony, which features a storage closet and overlooks the green inner gardens. The master bedroom at the rear is spacious and provides access to the northwest-facing balcony through French doors.'),
      (52,'Tolstraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 20, 4, 3, 66, 550, true,
      E'In a quiet part of Tolstraat, this 66-sqm living space, two-bedroom flat is coming up for sale. A French balcony, ceiling ornaments, a living room en-suite, several built-in cupboards, beautiful panel doors with classic door fittings and a balcony facing north-west make this an attractive and nice flat.\n\n'
       'The flat is located on the second floor and accessed via a communal staircase. The flat has recently been partially renovated. The renovation includes a new laminate floor, all interior painting and new electrical sockets.\n\n'
       'The kitchen is equipped with built-in appliances in the form of an oven, extractor hood, 5-burner and gas cooker. From the kitchen and from one of the bedrooms there is access to the balcony which is located on the northwest. Extra convenient is the cupboard in the hall with connection for the washing machine.\n\n'
       'Features:\n\n- Measurement report\n- Balcony facing north-west\n- Energy label D\n- Perpetual ground rent recorded with the notary\n- Small & active unit\n- VvE service costs approx. € 49,- per month\n- Central heating boiler renewed in 2022\n- non-self-occupation clause\n- ageing clause'),
      (53,'Amstelkade', 'APARTMENT', 10, 21, 3, 2, 66, 525, true,
      E'Bright and stylish 3-room apartment of approx. 65m² along the Amstel Canal, on the border of the Rivierenbuurt and De Pijp. Situated on the 3rd floor, it features a sunny south-facing balcony. At the front, enjoy the tranquil view of the water with the afternoon sun on your face. Delight in the lively scene of rowers and boats from nearby associations bringing the water to life.\n\n'
       'DETAILS\n* Unobstructed view over the Amstelkade\n* South-facing balcony\n* Two bedrooms\n* Separate toilet\n* Built-in cabinets on the balcony\n* Ground lease bought off until 2063\n* Fully renovated in 2016\n* Almost always a parking space available in the street\n* Equipped with a bathtub'),
      (54,'Stadionweg', 'APARTMENT', 10, 22, 4, 3, 114, 850, true,
      E'In a fantastic location in Amsterdam South, this spacious flat of 114m² is located on the fourth floor with a lovely balcony overlooking the beautiful courtyard garden. The flat is part of the ‘MUZENHOF’ complex in an ideal location: just outside the city centre, in the Beethoven neighbourhood in the highly sought-after district of Oud-Zuid, near the WTC, Beatrixpark and arterial roads. There are various shops, cosy cafés and restaurants in Beethovenstraat and various (international) schools are within walking distance.\n\n'
       'Fourth floor: private entrance with access to the hall. At the front the bright living room with access to the first balcony. Also located at the front is the first bedroom. This flat has two bathrooms. The first bathroom is equipped with a shower, sink and washing machine connection. The second bedroom located at the rear of the property has its own bathroom. It is equipped with a toilet, washbasin and shower. Also located at the rear are the closed kitchen and the third bedroom. Through the kitchen and the third bedroom you can also reach the large balcony overlooking the courtyard garden. There is also a separate toilet in the hallway.\n\n'
       'The non-binding information shown on this website has been carefully compiled by us based on information provided by the seller and/or third parties. We do not guarantee its accuracy or completeness. We advise you to contact us if you are interested in one of our properties or to have your own NVM estate agent assist you.'),
      (55,'Overtoom', 'APARTMENT', 10, 23, 3, 2, 80, 680, true,
      E'The property consists of an apartment on the second floor of approximately 80m² and 4 adjacent storage rooms on the fourth floor of approximately 41m² in total. This offers the possibility of transforming the storerooms into a house.\n\n'
       'This bright apartment is located on a beautiful part of the Overtoom and contains an area of approximately 80m², is located a few meters from the cozy and also beautiful Vondelpark, on the Overtoom. The house is completely casco and has a beautiful ceiling height of approx. 2,88m.\n\n'
       'PARTICULARS:\n- Total area of approx. 80m²\n- Spacious storage of a total of approx. 41m² on the attic floor, expandable with an entrance on the third floor;\n- Located on private land, so no leasehold\n- All windows are double glazed\n- The ''As Is'' and Non-residential clause applies\n- Owners Association consists of 4 members\n- In 2020, € 247,000 has been invested in the complete renovation of the facade. (Cost overview is in documentation)\n- Delivery in consultation, can be quick!'),
      (56,'Rooseveltlaan', 'APARTMENT', 10, 24, 4, 3, 140, 950, true,
      E'You reach the private entrance on the first floor of the building via a stone staircase. The corner location provides plenty of natural light. The living spaces are on the second, third, and fourth floors, making it a comfortable family home with three large bedrooms and two bathrooms.On the second floor, you’ll find a sunny and bright living room at the front with windows spanning the entire width. At the rear are a spacious bedroom and a large kitchen-diner. The living room and kitchen-diner are separated from the central hallway by beautiful beveled glass double doors. Both the kitchen-diner and the bedroom have doors leading to the balcony, which is northwest-facing. Between the living room and the kitchen, there is a bathroom with a bathtub, a shower corner, a vanity unit, and a cupboard for a washer and dryer, as well as a separate toilet.\n'
       'On the third mezzanine floor, there is a spacious bedroom with built-in wardrobes.Finally, on the fourth and top floor, there is a modern second bathroom with a walk-in shower, vanity unit, and a Sanibroyeur toilet, as well as a bright and spacious bedroom at the front.\n\n'
       'DETAILS\n• Living area: 139.7 m² (NEN2580 measurement report available)\n• Northwest-facing balcony\n• Three bedrooms, two bathrooms\n• Ground lease paid off until March 16, 2055\n• Delivery in consultation\n• Buyer chooses the notary in Amsterdam, following the Ring Amsterdam model'),
      (57,'Haarlemmer Houttuinen', 'APARTMENT', 10, 25, 2, 1, 34, 300, true,
      E'Super nice studio on a top location in the Haarlemmerbuurt! In a quiet part of the street around the corner from the lovely Haarlemmerdijk, the Haarlemmerstraat & the Jordaan. The studio is located on the third floor and has lots of (double) glass in the front facade, double doors with a French balcony and a nice unobstructed view. At the back of the building is a large communal and green garden facing south-west and a covered bicycle shed. Haarlemmer Houttuinen 45 was designed by architect Herman Zeinstra, founder of Dok architects and one of the Netherlands'' leading architects.\n\n'
       'Its location in the city centre is sublime. In the lee of tourism and within walking distance of everything: Noordermarkt, Westermarkt, Prinseneiland, Bickerseiland and Realeneiland, Central Station, the Amsterdam canals, Westerpark, cafes, restaurants, supermarkets, shops, cinemas and theatres.\n\n'
       'DETAILS\n-34 m²\n-double glazed\n-energy label B\n-french balcony front side\n-kitchen with work island/ drinks bar\n-built in 1984\n-concrete floor with light coloured wooden decking\n-lots of light\n-design by award-winning architect Herman Zeinstra\n-communal garden and bicycle shed\n-professional management Het Nieuwe VvE Beheer B.V.\n-MAJOP available\n-top location\n-ground rent bought off until 15-06-2034\n-Request for (favourable) transfer to perpetual leasehold has been made\n-exemption from transfer tax (see conditions website of the central government);'),
      (58,'Van Bossestraat', 'APARTMENT', 10, 26, 3, 2, 58, 550, true,
      E'Welcome to this spacious apartment located on the top two floors, in the quiet and popular Staatsliedenbuurt in Amsterdam. The house offers a spacious living room, two bedrooms and a sunny roof terrace. With the Westerpark within walking distance and various restaurants nearby, you can enjoy an ideal combination of peace and liveliness. Curious? Contact us quickly to schedule a viewing!\n\n'
       'DETAILS\n- 58 m2 (NEN measured);\n- Top floor apartment with sunny roof terrace;\n- Spacious living room with open kitchen;\n- Two bedrooms;\n- Beautiful wooden floor;\n- Leasehold bought off until 30-06-2056;\n- Service costs VVE € 216,-;\n- Delivery in consultation.'),
      (59,'Insulindeweg', 'APARTMENT', 10, 27, 4, 3, 98, 750, true,
      E'Living in the project ''De Smaragd'', built in 2014, is located in a special place in the city, right on the transition from the nineteenth-century buildings and the buildings from 1920-1940, architectural style the Amsterdam School. Energy label A, storage and a private indoor parking space. Perpetual leasehold has been bought off! In short, living in comfort!\n\n'
       'The architecture of these two periods is very different. When designing the Smaragd, the architect was inspired by both architectural periods. Amsterdam East is booming and this is reflected in the lively neighborhood where new and diverse catering establishments open every day. The location of this apartment is therefore top!\n'
       'The apartment is located at the beginning of the Insulindeweg, within walking distance of, among others, the Dappermarkt, the Tropenmuseum, the Oosterpark, Artis, the Javastraat and Brouwerij ''t IJ. For your daily shopping you can go to the Dapperstraat, the well-sorted shopping centre Oostpoort or the Eerste and Tweede van Swindenstraat and for various cafés, restaurants and eateries you can indulge yourself at the vibrant Javastraat and of course the well-known Linnaeusstraat (De Biertuin, Louie Louie, Pata Negra). From this location you will not be bored for a moment and you are everywhere in no time!\n\n'
       'DETAILS\n- Living area of approx. 98m² (according to NEN-2580)\n- Corresponding parking space in the basement below € 45,000,-\n- Three good size bedrooms\n- Energy label A\n- Year of construction 2015\n- Own storage room in the basement\n- Large & active VvE\n- VvE contribution apartment € 159.67\n- VvE contribution parking space € 56.60\n- Municipal leasehold has been bought off in perpetuity!\n- Seller has requested the favorable conditions in time\n- Delivery in consultation, can be done quickly!'),
      (60,'Waldenlaan', 'APARTMENT', 10, 28, 3, 2, 81, 650, true,
      E'Do you want the best of both worlds? At this cool apartment in the heart of Oostpoort with your own parking space in the garage!'
       'Welcome to Waldenlaan! Here you live in the vibrant heart of Oostpoort, in a top location with everything within reach. This apartment from 2014 is ready to move in and modernly finished, with 2 spacious bedrooms, energy label A+ and underfloor heating in every room. Enjoying the outdoors? Your balcony borders the shopping street. Can you see yourself enjoying the view? In addition, you can of course also use the courtyard, where you can really relax. And how nice: you have your own parking space in the parking garage. Here you will find the best of both worlds: the coziness of restaurants and terraces around the corner and the tranquility of the green parks nearby.\n\n'
       'Let''s put everything in a row\n- Own parking space in the parking garage\n- Fantastic location in the vibrant heart of Oostpoort\n- Apartment from 2014\n- 2 very spacious bedrooms\n- Ready to move in and neatly finished\n- Best of all worlds: restaurants around the corner and close to the parks\n- Energy label A+\n- Underfloor heating throughout the apartment\n- Cool courtyard as an extension of your balcony\n- Indoor access to the supermarket\n- Annual canon period June 16, 2025 to June 15, 2026. Parking space is €71.59 Apartment is €1627.78 and is indexed annually.');
